- op: discuss  # 8821
  at: '2026-05-31T09:45:31Z'  # 8821
  by: agent  # 8821
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 8821
  clock: 8  # 8821
  nonce: '8821'  # 8821
  message: "Scope re-evaluation 2026-05-31 (post-WI-huzuv merge + post-WI-kaziv data-gap collection). The original ~90-analyzer scope sketch was wrong on inspection — empirical grep + per-analyzer external-target edge counts produced a 22-analyzer residual with a tractable prioritization. Tier 1 (mechanical, sweep-equivalent): groovy — same shape as java/kotlin already-retrofitted analyzers; path_hint already in scope at the unresolved-call site; expected to be a single-PR follow-up. NB data shows low call-edge volume on the spring-boot rep but the data path is trivially-shippable. Tier 2 (per-analyzer threading work in lang-mainstream, ranked by unresolved-call-edge volume): lua (6893 unresolved per medium repo — HIGHEST PRIORITY), tcl (403), objc/perl/powershell (no data — large-repo or representative-failure blocker). Tier 3 (lang-extended1, ranked by data where available): d_lang (1121), pascal (73), plus 15 audit-pending — ada/asm/cobol/fennel/fish/gdscript/gleam/haxe/janet/nim/odin/pony/solidity/tcl-already-tier2/v_lang. Full data at /tmp/wi-nigah-data/summary.json (per-language counts of total edges, calls, unresolved, dst_ref percentage). Closing WI-huzuv (PR #3991 merged 2026-05-31) handled the 4 mechanical-sweep candidates that had module_hint at the emit site (kotlin/php/scala/swift); groovy is the 5th mechanical-equivalent. The remaining analyzers need per-analyzer threading of import-tracker output through to make_unresolved_edge — substantively similar to what WI-mafik did for the 7 originally-retrofitted analyzers. Status flips from needs_human_review to todo_soft per the original trigger condition."  # 8821
