  message: "WI-nigah Tier 1 + Tier 2 sweep complete 2026-05-31.\n\nShipped (in order):\n- Tier 1 — groovy retrofit (PR merged, threads path_hint from import_aliases)\n- Tier 2 — lua retrofit (PR merged, threads require_aliases via 2 call sites + coherence-fix for qualified dst)\n- Tier 2 — tcl retrofit (PR merged, rpartition(\"::\") namespace-split)\n- Tier 2 — objc retrofit (PR merged, _extract_message_receiver + PascalCase-receiver heuristic)\n- Tier 2 — perl retrofit (PR merged, rpartition(\"::\") package-split)\n- Tier 2 — powershell retrofit (PR merged, rpartition(\"\\\\\") module-split)\n\nAlso delivered alongside (PR #3995): WI-zisov Phase 2 polyglot-fixture audit, 5 new language fixtures with strict xfail markers documenting the analyzer gaps that future fix-side PRs will flip XPASSED.\n\nRemaining WI-nigah scope (not delivered in this round):\n- Tier 3 lang-extended1 long-tail (d_lang 1121 unresolved/repo, pascal 73, plus 15 audit-pending: ada/asm/cobol/fennel/fish/gdscript/gleam/haxe/janet/nim/odin/pony/solidity/v_lang). User scope-bounded today to Tier 1 + Tier 2 only.\n- Closing the WI-zisov xfail gaps (kotlin qualified-call, scala qualified-call, php static-method, csharp no-external-edges) — those are downstream analyzer-deepening work, not in this retrofit's shape.\n\nSuggest leaving WI-nigah at todo_soft pending the Tier 3 work, OR splitting into a separate Tier 3 umbrella + closing this one done. Not closing as 'done' here pending that decision."  # 0d35
